From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:11:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcxx: provide what GCC 12 and 13 lack from GCC 14 and 15

llvm 21 uses compiler builtins that GCC added in versions 14 and 15.
Add fallbacks for them, keeping the original code for compilers that
provide the builtins.

The type trait builtins, such as __is_array, __is_const, __remove_cv
and __decay, get template based implementations. The ones GCC added in
14 are selected by _LIBCPP_GCC_VER < 1400. The ones it only added in
15 are selected by __has_builtin, since GCC 14 lacks them as well.

__builtin_clzg, __builtin_ctzg and __builtin_popcountg dispatch to the
__builtin_clz, __builtin_ctz and __builtin_popcount variants.

__type_pack_element gets a recursive template in tuple_element.h,
make_tuple_types.h and variant.

__builtin_operator_new and __builtin_operator_delete, which only Clang
has, become ::operator new and ::operator delete.

is_void.h and is_null_pointer.h use __remove_cv_t instead of calling
the __remove_cv builtin.

bitset silences a false -Wstringop-overflow in to_string() from GCC 13.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
